        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "## Done — INI parser implemented, all tests pass\n\n### What I built\nA genuine line-scanning INI parser + printer in MoonBit, in the root `ini` package, split by concern (each file well under the 1000-line limit):\n\n| File | Lines | Role |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `errors.mbt` | 18 | `ParseError(Int32, String)` suberror + `Show` (`line 3: unterminated quoted value`) |\n| `scanner.mbt` | 146 | physical-line splitting (LF/CRLF), whitespace classes, separator lookup, odd/even trailing-backslash counting, inline-comment cut |\n| `value.mbt` | 125 | quoted/unquoted carrier, per-carrier escape table, closing-quote-on-same-line and text-after-quote checks |\n| `section.mbt` | 66 | `[name]`, nested-bracket rejection, wrapping-quote stripping, trailing text/comment rule |\n| `parser.mbt` | 146 | line loop, key validation (empty / whitespace-only / control chars), continuation joining, `global`/`sections` bookkeeping |\n| `printer.mbt` | 78 | `print` with double-quoted values (escapes `\\ \" \\n \\r \\t`) and quoted header form when a name needs it |\n\nNothing is fixture-specific: sections, keys, comments, quoting, escapes and continuations are all decided by grammar rules on raw text, and a continuation line is treated as pure text (its `=`, `:`, quotes and `;`/`#` are literal), exactly as `specs/ini.md` requires.\n\n### Validation actually run\n- `moon test` after `moon clean` (fresh build): **44 tests, 44 passed, 0 failed** — the 12 public cases plus 32 tests I added (`ini_entries_test.mbt`, `ini_value_test.mbt`, `ini_invalid_test.mbt`, `ini_samples_test.mbt`, `ini_property_test.mbt`), covering the escape table, the trailing-backslash run table, comment rules, section re-opening/last-wins, CRLF, malformed headers/keys/quotes/continuations, git-config/systemd/php.ini-shaped files, and 2000-case round-trip + 2000-case \"never panics\" property checks.\n- `moon check`: **clean** (0 errors, 0 warnings). `moon info`: interface up to date.\n- An independent explore-agent audit of the code against `specs/ini.md`; its two real findings were fixed and pinned by tests: (a) `print` now uses `[\"<name>\"]` for section names a bare header cannot reproduce, (b) text after a closing quote is judged on the first physical line, so continuation text there is an error instead of a silently dropped tail.\n\n### Notes / caveats\n- `moon fmt` was run; it also wants to apply a deprecated-syntax migration to the read-only `ini_spec.mbt` and a type rewrite to `ini_qc.mbt`. I reverted those two files to their delivered content (verified byte-identical modulo line endings), so `moon fmt --check` reports only those two protected files while all implementation files are formatted. `moon.pkg` gained a `for \"test\"` import for `moonbitlang/core/test` and warning settings that silence only the diagnostics those read-only files emit.\n- Where the spec leaves room, I chose and documented (in `README.md`): a comment after `[section]` is allowed but other trailing text is not; a continuation marker on the last line is an error (a trailing newline does not create a line to join); quoted syntax is decided on the first physical line only; an unquoted `;`/`#` starts a comment only after whitespace.\n- `README.md` (written from the code, not the spec) documents the architecture, the parsing pipeline, the design decisions, usage, and how to run the tests."
        }
