        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "I implemented a real INI parser in MoonBit for this repo's dialect.\n\n## What was built\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ini.mbt` | `parse`: line loop, section headers, entry storage in the global/section maps |\n| `scanner.mbt` | LF/CRLF line splitting, separator search, key validation, backslash-run counting |\n| `value.mbt` | value parsing: `\"…\"`/`'…'` carriers, per-carrier escapes, inline comments, continuations |\n| `printer.mbt` | `print`: always-quoted values, best-effort section-name quoting |\n| `error.mbt` | `IniError.Malformed` with line-numbered messages |\n| `ini_dialect_test.mbt` | 43 added tests: every rule in `specs/ini.md`, real-world samples, print round trips, 3000-case fuzz |\n\nPipeline: `text → lines → classify (blank/comment/section/entry) → key + value → Doc`, and the reverse for printing. Continuations are resolved on raw lines **before** escape decoding (odd/even trailing-backslash runs), inline comments are cut from the first line's raw text only (so a continuation line contributes text, not syntax), and values are trimmed before escapes are decoded. `print` emits `key = \"value\"` with `\\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\t` escaped, so any value round-trips.\n\n## Validation actually run\n\n- `moon test` → **55/55 pass** (12 shipped public tests incl. both property tests, plus my 43).\n- `moon check` → 0 errors; the only 3 warnings come from protected/given files (`derive(...)` in `ini_spec.mbt`, `test_unqualified_package` in `ini_pub_test.mbt`, unused `core/test` import in `moon.pkg`). My own five source files are diagnostic-free.\n- `moon fmt --check` → all files I own are formatter-clean; the only disagreements are in the two given files that shipped in the pre-migration style (`#derive`, `Int`→`Int32`). **Note:** `moon fmt` initially rewrote `ini_spec.mbt` and `ini_qc.mbt`; I reverted both to their original text so the do-not-modify set is intact (verified line-by-line against my initial reads).\n- `moon info` → regenerated `pkg.generated.mbti` (now lists `IniError` besides the required `parse`/`print`/`Doc`).\n- An independent review subagent audited the sources against `specs/ini.md` with ~140 targeted probes; it found one real inconsistency (closing `]` located with `rev_find`, so header acceptance depended on the trailing comment's text). I fixed it: section headers are now exact — the line must end with `]`, nothing (not even a comment) may follow, and brackets inside the name are rejected — which is the spec's literal grammar. It also found two over-claiming `print` doc comments and one narrow whitespace predicate, all corrected.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- The dialect leaves a few corners unspecified; I chose documented, defensible readings: a continuation marker at end of input is an error even when the input ends with a line break; a section header takes no trailing comment; unquoted values are trimmed on the raw text before escapes are decoded. Section/key names containing brackets or a leading `;`/`#` cannot be produced by `parse` and are outside the printing contract (documented in `print`)."
        }
